        <tr id="comment-body-516730"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://girlscouts.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A814e1a88-0b5e-43b7-9528-7a68556fa5b5" class="user-hover" rel="712020:814e1a88-0b5e-43b7-9528-7a68556fa5b5" data-account-id="712020:814e1a88-0b5e-43b7-9528-7a68556fa5b5" accountid="712020:814e1a88-0b5e-43b7-9528-7a68556fa5b5" rel="noreferrer">Kelly Kennedy</a> - Please review and approve</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-516938"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:814e1a88-0b5e-43b7-9528-7a68556fa5b5"
                id="word_commented_712020:814e1a88-0b5e-43b7-9528-7a68556fa5b5"
                href="https://girlscouts.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A814e1a88-0b5e-43b7-9528-7a68556fa5b5">
                    Kelly Kennedy
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">30/Jun/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-516938"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://girlscouts.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=62ed05c125abc07e51c69f8c" class="user-hover" rel="62ed05c125abc07e51c69f8c" data-account-id="62ed05c125abc07e51c69f8c" accountid="62ed05c125abc07e51c69f8c" rel="noreferrer">Priya Singh</a>  I have a few clarification questions on this ticket:</p>

<ol>
	<li>Can you help me understand why this is classified as an <b>EDS</b> ticket? Since there are no authoring requirements and the breadcrumb is dynamically generated from the Commerce taxonomy, I would have expected this to be a Commerce storefront component rather than an EDS feature.</li>
	<li>Is the scope of this ticket limited to the commerce pages listed (PLP, PDP, Cart, Checkout)? In our designs, I recall breadcrumbs also appearing on pages such as <b>My Account</b>. If those pages are intended to have breadcrumbs as well, should they be included here or covered by a separate ticket?</li>
	<li>I noticed a potential inconsistency in the mobile breadcrumb behavior. The acceptance criteria describe the collapsed format as <b>Home &gt; … &gt; Current</b>, while the functional details state that the <b>parent category remains clickable</b>. Could we clarify the intended behavior? From a usability perspective, preserving the immediate parent (when possible) seems like the better experience since it allows users to easily navigate back one level.</li>
</ol>

        </td></tr>
